WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.897
The GROUP BY versus PARTITION BY choice is fundamentally a grain decision.

00:00:04.897 --> 00:00:09.472
If you want one row per patient, GROUP BY may be correct.

00:00:09.472 --> 00:00:15.267
If you need every admission and the patient average beside it, a window is a better fit.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:19.112
Ask whether detail should be collapsed or preserved.

00:00:19.112 --> 00:00:23.522
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:28.922
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:28.922 --> 00:00:32.652
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:32.652 --> 00:00:37.227
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:37.227 --> 00:00:44.407
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:44.407 --> 00:00:48.507
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project:

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:53.059
validate the meaning of the result, not only whether the statement executes.
